SUMMARY:Beyond the Telling
DESCRIPTION:This dance performance invites audiences to experience familiar stories from unexpected perspectives. Through an original movement vocabulary\, Shilpanatanam\, the evening showcases five stories that explore creation\, perception\, duality\, grief\, and celebration. A new vocabulary\, a new lens on old stories. \nThe evening opens with Vimarsha Samarpana\, an offering of thought embodied through AUM (Om)\, the primordial creative impulse from which all creation emerges. In Then the Boundless Roared\, the Narasimha narrative shifts from spectacle to darshan\, the experience of beholding the divine. Tara explores the duality of the feminine divine\, where ferocity and compassion coexist. In Kalidasa’s Rati Vilaap\, Rati’s grief takes centre stage through the intimate lens of a woman’s sorrow. The evening concludes with Gajjar\, where two pilgrims on the road to Pandharpur turn their journey into a joyful contest of storytelling. \nCredits:\nChoreography: Maya Kulkarni\nPerformance: Kaustavi Sarkar & Deepa Mahadevan\nDance Vocabulary: Shilpanatanam — Dramaturgy in Motion \nSupported by: \n \n\n\nFamiliar Stories. Unfamiliar Turns.\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSf-5TfS9gtyZ0Z1lAW1efIW1ywMtT9m3cn1dIT8xkPZ-9TQBQ/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Performers*: Maya Kulkarni\, Kaustavi Sarkar\, Deepa Mahadevan\n*Event Categories*: Dance\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/beyond-the-telling/
LOCATION:7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bengaluru\, Karnataka\, 560 071\, India
CATEGORIES:Dance,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail-25.jpg
