SUMMARY:Rediscovering the Hometown
DESCRIPTION:Shillong is a historical landscape\, not only a natural one. \nBased on the book Hometown: Shillong in the World\, this conversation examines the city’s layered past to illuminate larger questions of identity\, modernity\, and belonging in contemporary India\, followed by an audience Q&A. What is there to know about Shillong beyond its hills? \nThe session takes a deep dive into a small city that began as a British hill station\, later became the capital of Assam\, and is now the capital of Meghalaya. It follows nostalgia for imagined utopias\, the aspirations and confusions of the city’s young\, its music scene\, its politics and violence\, and the growth of both evangelical religion and consumerist desire. Combining thorough research with rigorous reporting\, the book skilfully maps the lives and histories that have shaped Shillong. \nVenue: Library\n\n\nA New Biography of Shillong\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdu37BrKD26xIQaUHPGncez5QrzI5h6g4pi16uj4fzkGblgZQ/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Anjum Hasan\, Nandini Nair\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Cities\, Heritage
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/rediscovering-the-hometown/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Cities,Heritage
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail-29.jpg
