SUMMARY:The Unlikely History of Bengaluru
DESCRIPTION:\nBengaluru was not built in a day. \nThis lecture explores the discoveries\, encounters\, and historical connections that shaped the city as it stands today\, drawing on the book Bengaluru: The Comprehensive History to the Dawn of Independence. Most accounts begin in 1537\, with Kempe Gowda\, but what was already in motion before he arrived? \nThe city’s creation was the outcome of thousands of years of unfolding history. By 1537\, the ground had been set: first by the geology that shaped the Deccan Plateau\, then by the geography that determined its trade routes\, and finally by the people\, kingdoms\, merchants\, and armies who moved across this landscape. Each left something behind. Together\, they created the conditions for a city to emerge. \n\nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nA City Made of Countless Consequences\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd4T35faJEsmM9hEUgdgmHovVDzZE5uEcQr09w5mDvAE7RXcg/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Ramjee Chandran\, Chiranjiv Singh\n*Event Categories*: Bangalore\, Books\, Culture\, Heritage\, History\, Nonfiction\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-unlikely-history-of-bengaluru/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Bangalore,Books,Culture,Heritage,History,Nonfiction,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/ThumbnailRamje.jpg
END:VEVENT
