SUMMARY:In Search of the Snow Leopard
DESCRIPTION:Wildlife researcher Munib Khanyari and artist Nirupa Rao discuss their new book\, The Lost Snow Leopard: A Himalayan Adventure\, in conversation with conservationist and scientist Charudutt (Charu) Mishra\, who brings with him three decades of experience in the field\, across High Asia. \nThe book commemorates the first ever estimation of snow leopards in Jammu & Kashmir led by Munib\, Kulbhushansingh Suryawanshi and their colleagues from the Nature Conservation Foundation\, in collaboration with the J&K Wildlife Department. The survey helped ‘find’ the region’s snow leopards; decades of regional conflict had made them exceptionally difficult to study\, and effectively ‘lost’ to science. Playing on this allusion\, The Lost Snow Leopard celebrates Munib’s landmark research\, transforming it into an illustrated work of narrative fiction that can be shared with a wider audience of all age groups. \nMunib and Charu share fascinating\, firsthand experience of tracking and conserving snow leopards in some of the world’s most challenging terrains\, while Nirupa gives us a behind-the-scenes look into combining science and storytelling in the making of the book\, and her artistic process. \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nScience and Storytelling \nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLScawNaIEiDeDZNSf6Y2F6MnqnjUzHW1GLCkxHho6MbR7PERkQ/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Nirupa Rao\, Munib Khanyari\, Charudutt Mishra\n*Event Categories*: Environment\, Literature\, Photography\, Visual Arts\, Wildlife
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/in-search-of-the-snow-leopard/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Environment,Literature,Photography,Visual Arts,Wildlife
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_nirupa.jpg
END:VEVENT
