SUMMARY:The German Musical Legacy
DESCRIPTION:This piano recital celebrates the German musical legacy through the works of Bach\, Beethoven\, and Brahms\, with a special interlude by Claude Debussy. The pianist approaches each piece as a painter might a canvas\, creating art through melody and rhythm. \nThe programme moves from some of Bach’s and Schumann’s most emblematic piano pieces to Debussy’s “Reflections in the Water” and Beethoven’s deeply expressive Piano Sonata in E major\, Op. 109. After a Christmas piece by Liszt\, the evening culminates in Brahms’s dazzling Paganini Variations\, Op. 35 (Book I). \nPresented by: \n \nSupported by:\n    \nAccess contact information for Furtados here. \nVenue: Auditorium\n\n\nCelebrating the Works of Bach\, Beethoven\, Brahms\nRSVPs will open on Thu\, Nov 26 at 6pm.\n*Performer*: Andreas König\n*Event Categories*: Music\, Performing Arts
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/the-german-musical-legacy/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Music,Performing Arts
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_GML.jpg
END:VEVENT
