SUMMARY:Cradle to Grave: Welfare in India
DESCRIPTION:Based on the book Freebies or Rights\, this discussion examines how social policy actually shapes everyday life: from school meals and the Public Distribution System to maternity benefits and the rural employment guarantee. Is state-provided support simply a set of “freebies” or is it the right that makes a dignified life possible? \nDrawing on over two decades of field research across rural India\, the book moves beyond political rhetoric through stories from villages\, classrooms\, and government offices\, raising the question of why protections treated as essentials in many countries are so often dismissed as handouts in India. It asks whether welfare programmes create dependency or expand freedom and opportunity\, presenting social protection not as charity but as a foundation for dignity\, justice\, and democratic life. \nVenue: Gallery\n\n\nHow Social Policies Shape Lives\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSd47eO5Ph6LPLCEeri7khZdycKQe_nBDcLAflXTQPUoRjIc1Q/viewform?usp=publish-editor)\n*Speakers*: Reetika Khera\, Aakar Patel\n*Event Categories*: Policy & Regulation\, Politics\, Public Health\, Society
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/cradle-to-grave-welfare-in-india/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Policy & Regulation,Politics,Public Health,Society
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Thumbnail_CtG.jpg
END:VEVENT
