SUMMARY:Smart Machines\, Wise Leaders
DESCRIPTION:Based on the book The Unartificial Leader\, this discussion asks what humans must hold onto as machines grow more capable. Drawing on interviews with CEOs\, founders\, and next-generation leaders\, the authors argue that intelligence and wisdom are not the same thing. \nThe book offers six imperatives\, from adaptive resilience to moral judgement\, as a framework for leading with clarity in an AI-augmented world: not a rejection of technology\, but an argument for deepening human maturity alongside it. Where does your agency sit as you embrace AI? \nVenue: Seminar Halls\n\n\nSix Imperatives for an AI-Augmented World\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdbYONvK8y92Jm5TajFX5KzKvuJ3zVEJVZW57Ev7hRacQlFog/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Swati Apte & Garima Deveshwar Bahl\, Shrikant Karwa\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Management\, Nonfiction\, Society\, Technology
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/smart-machines-wise-leaders/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Management,Nonfiction,Society,Technology
